d I pick us up at the  airport and I'm almost through it I  think that I'm not gonna call it a work  of genius and the thing is I disagree  profoundly with a lot of the stuff in  that in the book that I'm reading now  which is kind of supposed to be a  history of humankind going from you know  from  primitive days - - today I disagree  profoundly with a lot of it and this is  someone who would certainly  anti-religion for one thing and that  becomes very clear but there are some  sort of genius elements of it because  there are because in the book he for  instance a lot of the book is basically  a almost a polemic against the  agricultural revolution which is so I'm  reading that it was I don't really agree  you know I think the agricultural  revolution ten thousand years ago was a  good thing and it made human  civilization possible which is no sum no  small perk either but I don't think I've  ever heard anyone actually criticized  the Agricultural Revolution that's just  something we all take for granted well  yeah agriculture of course that's good  we need that so in this book at least  through part of it he he's basically  arguing that we'd be better if it never  happened in giving his reasons again I  don't agree with all the reasons but I  think that's sort of a a genius move in  a way be able to take something that  everyone else takes for granted make  some observations about it that other  people hadn't thought of and then make  people go oh but I just hadn't thought  of it that way  alright so we'll leave it there thanks  everybody for watching Godspeed in the  wake of Fredo Cuomo's meltdown many  prominent conservatives are taking CNN  side and President Trump is furious  about that  then another CNN scandal this time  involving Don Lemon and it takes place  at one of my favorite bars in New York  we'll go into that an evangelical  musician loses his faith and finally  more details emerge in the Jeffrey  Epstein saga check it out on a Michael  Knowles show
 

